{"name":"Emu Egg","hex":"#3d8481","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"emu","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Eastern Muria."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large flightless bird native to Australia, Dromaius novaehollandiae. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A cassowary (genus Casuarius)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emu"},{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food.","An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Emu","blocks":[{"text":"The emu is a species of flightless bird endemic to Australia, where it is the tallest native bird. It is the only extant member of the genus Dromaius and the third-tallest living bird after its African ratite relatives, the common ostrich and Somali ostrich. The emu's native ranges cover most of the Australian mainland. The Tasmanian, Kangaroo Island and King Island subspecies became extinct after the European settlement of Australia in 1788."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Emu_1_-_Tidbinbilla.jpg/330px-Emu_1_-_Tidbinbilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emu","wikidata":"Q93208"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg","wikidata":"Q17147"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Emu_skeleton.jpg/500px-Emu_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Emu_skeleton.jpg/500px-Emu_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mounted skeleton","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmu_skeleton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Dromaius_novaehollandiae_-zoo_-two_feet.jpg/500px-Dromaius_novaehollandiae_-zoo_-two_feet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Dromaius_novaehollandiae_-zoo_-two_feet.jpg/1280px-Dromaius_novaehollandiae_-zoo_-two_feet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Dromaius_novaehollandiae_-zoo_-two_feet.jpg/500px-Dromaius_novaehollandiae_-zoo_-two_feet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign